WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:10.950
--I decided to hold an opening party
for Bamboo Forest Laundry Service.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:16.500
--So that's why I'd like everyone
from the ducal family to join us.
--I decided to hold an opening party
for Bamboo Forest Laundry Service.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.290
--I decided to hold an opening party
for Bamboo Forest Laundry Service.

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.700
--I invited the people who've helped me out
because I wanted to show them my thanks.

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.870
--Yeah, I'll go for sure.
--I invited the people who've helped me out
because I wanted to show them my thanks.

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:27.080
--I invited the people who've helped me out
because I wanted to show them my thanks.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.910
We'll definitely go!

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.910
Oh, how nice. I will gladly attend.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.000
Yes, I look forward to seeing you!

00:02:07.950 --> 00:02:12.950
"Episode 8"
"Laundry Business, with the Slimes"

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.700
Are we getting closer?

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.370
Yes, it should be coming into view.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:24.250
That's the building there.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.200
"Even goblin grime"...

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.250
..."cleaned off for an affordable price"...

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.250
"Bamboo Forest Laundry Service"...

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.500
Good!

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.160
That should do.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:57.950
How are you doing, my lady?

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:03.410
Well, it's almost done.
I just have to wait for it to bake.

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.750
Then we're all set.

00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:12.120
My lady, Ms. Araune, Ms. Lilian,
thank you so much for helping.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.620
Please don't mention it.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:18.410
We will gladly help you
with anything, Mr. Ryoma.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:22.250
Please don't hesitate to ask if you need us.

00:03:25.040 --> 00:03:27.790
Mr. Ryoma! They're here!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.620
This impressive shop...

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:43.500
...was built by an 11-year-old
relative of the ducal family...?

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:49.000
Age is irrelevant. You must not
judge a person by their appearances.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:51.500
Try to control your preconceptions.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.500
Right.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.620
--Also, Mr. Ryoma is not a relative...

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.660
--Mr. Serge!
--Also, Mr. Ryoma is not a relative...

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.950
Welcome!

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.790
Hello.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:03.750
Congratulations on the completion of your shop.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.660
Thank you very much.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.330
Mr. Serge, are these the...

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.370
Yes, allow me to introduce them.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.870
These are your new assistants...

00:04:13.870 --> 00:04:17.200
My name is Carla Norad.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.040
My name is Callum Norad.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.000
I am Ryoma Takebayashi. It's a pleasure
to make your acquaintance.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.540
I am Eliaria Jamil.
I'm helping Mr. Ryoma today.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.830
Thank you for coming.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.870
My brother and I are at your service.

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:40.080
My sister and I are at your service.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:44.790
They are young, but they served as
sub-manager and deputy sub-manager

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:48.040
at the Luiam branch of our
Morgan Trading Company.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:49.160
Ah.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:52.950
I am confident that they will
be able to assist Mr. Ryoma.

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:59.000
Wonderful. All right, please follow me.
I'll show you the work process in this shop.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:06.080
First, we ask our customers to
purchase a sack to put their laundry in.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.000
There are several sizes, and they can
use it as many times as they want.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.080
Yes.

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.700
The laundry fees are charged per sack.
The prices differ by the size.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:20.830
Yes.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.040
After you accept their payment
and take their laundry,

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:28.750
please give them a claim check.

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:31.950
They'll need it to get their laundry back.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.370
Yes.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:36.870
Please put the sack you received in here.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:40.330
This room has the cleaner slimes...

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:43.620
Oh, did you hear about the cleaner slimes?

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.540
We have been told that
they are slimes that eat grime.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:51.830
Yes, that's correct. Any questions so far?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:56.700
We heard this is a new breed of slime.
Does it really clean well?

00:05:56.700 --> 00:06:00.040
How should we dry the laundry after cleaning?

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.200
And that's how it goes.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:36.370
Then you can put the laundry back
in the sack to return to the customer.

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:40.200
Do the cleaner slimes clean any type of grime?

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.410
I haven't come across anything
they can't clean yet,

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:48.370
but if possible, please double-check
before returning to the customer.

00:06:48.370 --> 00:06:50.000
Understood.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:56.040
Also, we call it laundry, but there's
no water involved, just slimes eating.

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:58.080
Therefore there's no need to dry.

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.500
Understood.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:04.120
That's the workflow here. Any questions?

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:06.290
None, at the moment.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:12.200
I see. Well, please don't hesitate
to ask if anything comes up.

00:07:12.200 --> 00:07:13.790
Understood.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:21.160
Are they dissatisfied with reception
and laundry-carrying duties?

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:24.200
They do seem to be
quite capable businesspeople...

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.870
Maybe they feel this work
is not good enough for them.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:33.830
This area is for employees only,
off-limits for customers.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:36.830
There's the dressing room,
guest meeting room, manager's office,

00:07:36.830 --> 00:07:42.450
a break area for employees,
a restroom, and the office kitchen.

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.000
Understood.

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.750
These are the dormitories.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:53.790
You're the first to live here,
so please choose any room you like.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:55.250
Understood.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.250
Hey! Ryo-mya!

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:03.250
Looks like everyone is here.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:09.120
Ms. Carla, Mr. Callum,
please help me with the party.

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:10.620
Understood.

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.200
Here you are, Mr. Ryoma.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.080
Thank you, my lady.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.790
This reminds me of the speech they
made me do in the office in the morning...

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:47.910
Nobody listened then...

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.290
Um, everyone,

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:59.950
thank you for attending
the opening party for Bamboo Forest.

00:08:59.950 --> 00:09:03.160
Ryo-mya, so grown up...

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.540
What role are you playing in this?

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.910
I would not have been able to
do this without your help.

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:13.290
Thank you very much.

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:18.700
As a small token of gratitude,
I have prepared some quick meals.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.910
Please enjoy.

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.830
Cheers!

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.160
Congratulations, Ryoma.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.950
Congratulations!

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.580
Thank you!

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:43.000
Is it fish?! I want it <i>meow</i>!

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:46.950
Yum, yum!

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:50.000
This really is good...
I could eat all of this myself!

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.500
What's this dirty old hag doing here?

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:57.290
Who are you calling dirty?
I might be an old hag, but I'm not dirty!

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:00.200
That's why you used to be such a...

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:04.330
Stop bringing up my past every time we meet!

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:08.000
Glissela, what about his past
were you trying to say?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.370
Well hello, Maylene. Well, this boy here,
one time, during a mission...

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:17.040
Hey! Stop! Maylene, you go eat over there!

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:19.290
Yes, yes, certainly.

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.580
Sheesh... Hey.

00:10:21.580 --> 00:10:23.830
What is it, clumsy boy?

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:30.200
What do you think about
Ryoma's business? You think it'll do well?

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:31.830
I'm sure it will.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:32.790
Seriously?

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:36.790
--I can't say exactly how well,
but it'll do fine.

00:10:36.790 --> 00:10:38.660
--Yes, thank you. Yes, I'll do my very best.
--I can't say exactly how well,
but it'll do fine.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:41.290
--Yes, thank you. Yes, I'll do my very best.
--Don't you want to give him
some tips or something?

00:10:41.290 --> 00:10:42.540
--Yes, thank you. Yes, I'll do my very best.
--For now, I'll just watch.

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:43.910
--Hey, kid, any more food coming?
--For now, I'll just watch.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:45.580
--Hey, kid, any more food coming?
--I'll let him do what he thinks is best.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:48.540
--Oh yes, there's plenty more!
--I'll let him do what he thinks is best.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:53.790
That said, if he asks for help,
I wouldn't be against offering it.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.000
You'd better watch over him properly, too.

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.500
Yeah, I know.

00:10:59.500 --> 00:11:02.290
He seems to have earned the trust of everyone.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:04.080
Yes, sister.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.910
Thank you!

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.870
So helpful.

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:10.580
Yes, indeed.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.830
Yes, looks good!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.580
It's very crispy.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.450
Mr. Reinhart, did you enjoy the food?

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.660
Yes, it was very delicious.

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:36.700
Really? I assumed you'd have experience
eating much better food at noble parties.

00:11:37.790 --> 00:11:40.000
Wh-What's wrong?

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:44.120
Ryoma, you should know one thing.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:45.500
Y-Yes...?

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:49.450
Expensive food isn't necessarily good...

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:56.750
I guess nobles have
their own share of problems...

00:11:56.750 --> 00:12:00.870
Mreow... I sure did eat. I'm full!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:03.000
I'm so glad I came!

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.330
Yeah, even I'm quite full now.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:10.000
Everyone, dessert is ready!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.450
I've been waiting for this!

00:12:11.450 --> 00:12:12.870
Always room for dessert!

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.910
Let's eat!

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.040
Looks delicious!

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.950
I'm glad they seem to be enjoying this.

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:23.700
And thus the opening party was a success.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.950
Mr. Callum, Ms. Carla,
thank you for your help today.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.750
You are welcome.

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:37.910
So... if you could continue to work with me
starting tomorrow, it would be great...

00:12:37.910 --> 00:12:41.330
But... if you don't feel like it, I...

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.250
About that,

00:12:43.250 --> 00:12:47.370
my brother and I have discussed earlier.

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:51.410
Please allow us to work here.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.290
Are you sure?

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:54.120
Yes.

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.910
We had strong worries at first.

00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:03.250
A business, run by an 11-year-old,
using slimes for laundry... But...

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:08.450
Those worries disappeared.
This shop, your personality,

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:12.750
and the trust and support
that so many people have in you...

00:13:12.750 --> 00:13:19.790
We believe we can learn a lot from you.
We would love to work here.

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:23.580
We hope to live up to the expectation of
Morgan Trading Company who introduced us...

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:28.830
And we will do our best to bring honor
to the Takebayashi family.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:33.790
I'm so glad to have someone with
great expertise in business on board.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.040
I look forward to working with you.

00:13:38.620 --> 00:13:39.750
Yes, sir!

00:13:40.910 --> 00:13:45.410
But please don't try too hard. Just be normal.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:49.540
Morgan Trading Company has a reputation,
but my family doesn't at all.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.620
It is the least we can do.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:56.750
Even the smallest bad reputation
can spread quickly among nobles.

00:13:56.750 --> 00:14:00.580
Huh? Why would nobles talk about my tiny shop?

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.160
Most nobles pay close attention
to the activities of other families.

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:11.250
Other families...?
Wait, do you think I'm a noble?

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:13.000
You aren't?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:17.080
We were told you were related
with the Jamil ducal family.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.290
And the lady was here, too...

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:25.790
Oh, um, they treat me well,
but I'm not a noble myself.

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:30.120
I'm sorry, I tried to explain earlier, but...

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:32.450
So you're not a noble?

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:38.080
Correct, I'm just an adventurer.
So please just be normal around me.

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:42.120
Understood.

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:45.000
All right, we'll be starting business tomorrow.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.040
Please rest well tonight!

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.040
Okay!

00:14:49.160 --> 00:14:52.370
If you drink that, your color will change.

00:14:53.660 --> 00:14:58.000
Rub, rub, squeak, squeak. Rub, rub.

00:15:05.080 --> 00:15:08.700
It's finally opening day for Bamboo Forest.

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:10.870
Will we get customers?

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.620
I'd better not get my hopes up too much.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:15.330
Good morning.

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:19.660
Manager, Lady Eliaria.

00:15:19.660 --> 00:15:22.750
Good morning.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.200
I look forward to working with you today.

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:35.330
Good.

00:15:35.330 --> 00:15:37.580
All ready.

00:15:37.580 --> 00:15:39.620
Ms. Carla, Mr. Callum.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:44.410
I doubt that we'd get any customers
right away, but please be ready.

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:48.830
I'll go to the Adventurer's Guild
to let them know we've opened.

00:15:48.830 --> 00:15:51.250
In that case, I'll take my leave as well.

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.750
Understood, have a safe trip.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.330
I'll be fine here.

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:57.620
Hmm? I can walk you to the inn.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:00.370
Don't worry. See?

00:16:02.040 --> 00:16:07.330
I see, magic training day. Good luck.

00:16:07.330 --> 00:16:09.500
Yes! You, too.

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:12.660
Mr. Ryoma!

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.790
Hey, Ryoma, you're opening today, right?

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:27.700
Huh?

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:30.160
I'll be visiting first thing after work today.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:34.500
Thank you, but um, how do you know?

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.450
How? Look.

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.410
"Ryoma's laundry service opening today"?!

00:16:43.410 --> 00:16:47.120
Miya and Welanna came by
earlier and put that up.

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:49.080
They did?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:52.500
They said they're going to
go advertise elsewhere, too.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:56.580
Anyway, see you after work, okay?

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:59.660
Y-Yes, thank you!

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:04.290
Oh, we do full-body washing as well,
including armor and weapons!

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:06.160
Please give it a try!

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:07.160
Got it!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:09.540
Right, well I should do something, too...

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.620
Herb gathering.

00:17:14.620 --> 00:17:17.700
I guess I can do that while I patrol the mines.

00:17:17.700 --> 00:17:18.700
Right.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:23.500
Ms. Maylene, I'd like to take this job.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:25.700
Hey, thanks for the food yesterday.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:28.000
Are you sure you want to
be doing jobs right now?

00:17:28.000 --> 00:17:28.870
Huh?

00:17:28.870 --> 00:17:31.910
Aren't you busy with lots of customers?

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:34.700
Oh, we won't get that many
customers on our first day.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:39.910
Are you sure? Oh well. Okay, off you go then.

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:40.910
Yes!

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:50.120
Nothing else seems out of place...

00:17:50.120 --> 00:17:53.330
I guess that's enough patrolling for today.

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:56.080
Are they done gathering herbs?

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:04.870
After patrolling the mines, I delivered
the herbs to the guild to collect my pay.

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:07.250
Then, I returned to my shop. And...

00:18:08.700 --> 00:18:10.290
What, what?!

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:12.700
I totally shouldn't have been
taking on jobs today!

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:14.950
I have to help!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.040
M-Manager?!

00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:23.290
What's going on?!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.830
Well, we're crying out in joy!

00:18:25.830 --> 00:18:28.950
There are many neighbors coming in.

00:18:28.950 --> 00:18:30.700
Wh-What?!

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:33.040
We've been waiting for you to open.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:36.250
Some adventurers told us about this place.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:41.620
You said you can clean goblin grime,
so I thought I'd give it a try.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:44.950
The pricing is good, too.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:46.830
Thank you!

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:50.250
Ms. Carla, Mr. Callum,
please help the customers here!

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:53.700
I will do all of the laundry hauling!

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:58.700
I guess this is a "cry of joy" situation.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.540
After this, we...

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.620
...kept working and working and working.

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:18.200
Thank you.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:20.000
You guys did well.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:23.750
That was quite a large turnout.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:27.950
Yes, I did not expect that at all,
so I'm very surprised.

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:33.290
There was not even a break in... Hey, wait!
Have you two had any time to rest?!

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:34.120
No.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:36.620
I'm sorry, I didn't notice!

00:19:36.620 --> 00:19:40.250
This is bad. I can't exploit my workforce!

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.370
I owe it to my previous life!

00:19:42.370 --> 00:19:46.200
Umm... I will hire more employees immediately!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:48.660
Assuming breaks are taken in shifts...

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:51.160
How about four... Or rather, six more people?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.620
That sounds good.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:58.040
I believe once word gets around about this shop,
we will see even more business.

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:04.750
If you talk to the Merchant's Guild,
they can introduce you to potential workers.

00:20:04.750 --> 00:20:09.660
Understood! I'll head over there right away!

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.000
Thank you.

00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:17.750
You two should get some rest as soon as
you're done calculating our sales.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:19.450
Thank you, and great work!

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:23.330
How was the first day?

00:20:23.330 --> 00:20:27.040
It was much busier than expected.
We were totally swamped.

00:20:27.950 --> 00:20:34.330
I knew you'd do well, but I didn't
expect it to be quite so explosive.

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:38.540
In that case, are you here
to find more employees?

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.500
You really catch on quick!

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:44.290
I haven't spent many long years
as an old hag for nothing.

00:20:44.290 --> 00:20:46.120
An old hag, for years?

00:20:46.120 --> 00:20:52.370
Got it. I'll gather some candidates.
You decide who to hire.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.750
Yes. Thank you!

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:57.830
Really, that many customers?

00:20:57.830 --> 00:20:59.330
A huge success.

00:20:59.330 --> 00:21:02.700
I'm not sure if it's a huge success.

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:07.080
If I disappoint the customers,
it could all be over.

00:21:07.080 --> 00:21:11.330
I'll work hard so that people would
want to visit us many times.

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:14.580
You'll be fine, I'm sure.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.200
You should visit the town guard's quarters.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:19.200
Hmm?

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.410
That place is packed with men.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:24.250
I'm sure it's full of unwashed laundry.

00:21:24.250 --> 00:21:27.700
It might be a good source of
stable income for you.

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:30.620
I will do that. Thank you.

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:33.870
You must be tired. Go ahead and rest.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:38.410
Yes. This was all very new to me.
I am quite tired.

00:21:39.790 --> 00:21:41.870
Mr. Ryoma.

00:21:41.870 --> 00:21:44.330
Good night!

00:21:44.330 --> 00:21:46.790
Good night, my lady.

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.700
Wow, I am tired. But...

00:21:58.540 --> 00:22:00.250
We're alone again!

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:02.580
Shut up and work.

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:06.750
Back then, I used to sleep like
a dead man, no thoughts at all.

00:22:09.830 --> 00:22:12.450
Now, even if I'm tired from work...

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:16.250
...it feels so comfortable...
